From: =?UTF-8?q?Lu=C3=ADs=20Duarte?= <lduarte@cloudflare.com>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 12:30:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Keep color-scheme: normal light

Upstream resolves light-dark() and the dark system colors against
color-scheme (Bug 2068247, "Support color-scheme in Servo"), but lets
`normal` follow the device preference. Keep `normal` light, since dark
is opt-in per css-color-adjust. A value naming exactly one scheme still
wins outright, and `light dark` defers to the device's
prefers-color-scheme.
---
 device/servo.rs | 8 +++++---
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/device/servo.rs b/device/servo.rs
index a8f94bf..ac9fc4a 100644
--- a/device/servo.rs
+++ b/device/servo.rs
@@ -344,9 +344,11 @@ impl Device {
             return supports_dark_mode;
         }

-        // If either both or none are supported, then use the preferred color scheme
-        // to determine whether the user wants dark mode.
-        return self.color_scheme() == PrefersColorScheme::Dark;
+        // If both are supported, use the preferred color scheme to
+        // determine whether the user wants dark mode. If neither is (`normal`),
+        // stay light: dark is opt-in per
+        // <https://drafts.csswg.org/css-color-adjust/#color-scheme-prop>.
+        supports_dark_mode && self.color_scheme() == PrefersColorScheme::Dark
     }

     pub(crate) fn system_color(
